---
import { REPO_URL } from "../lib/releases";
---

<section class="section faq" id="faq">
  <div class="container faq-grid">
    <div class="faq-head">
      <h2>Before you install.</h2>
      <p class="section-lead">
        peekr is a small, local-first tool. The full documentation lives in the repository.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href={`${REPO_URL}/tree/main/docs`}>Read the docs</a>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-list">
      <details>
        <summary>Is peekr free?</summary>
        <p>Yes. MIT licensed and source public. No telemetry or paid tier.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Where are my access tokens stored?</summary>
        <p>The OS keychain, one entry per account. Never in config or logs.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Which providers can I connect?</summary>
        <p>Bitbucket Cloud and GitHub, with any number of accounts.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Does it update itself?</summary>
        <p>No. Settings, About, Check for updates opens the release page. Nothing installs.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Why are the builds unsigned?</summary>
        <p>No Apple Developer ID or Windows certificate. Verify <code>SHA256SUMS</code>.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
